{
  "tema": 5263,
  "slug": "trabajaba-imperfecto-ar",
  "titulo": "-ar verbs in the imperfect",
  "subtitulo": "De niño, surfeaba todos los días.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "To form the imperfect of an -ar verb, drop -ar and add -aba, -abas, -aba, -ábamos, -aban. Every -ar verb is regular in the imperfect, and only nosotros has a written accent.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The imperfect describes the past as **ongoing or repeated**: what you **used to do** or **were doing**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "trabaj-",
            "+",
            "-aba / -abas / -aba / -ábamos / -aban"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Ending",
            "trabajar",
            "jugar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**-aba**",
              "trabajaba",
              "jugaba"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**-abas**",
              "trabajabas",
              "jugabas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "**-aba**",
              "trabajaba",
              "jugaba"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**-ábamos**",
              "trabajábamos",
              "jugábamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ustedes",
              "**-aban**",
              "trabajaban",
              "jugaban"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**No exceptions** for -ar verbs: no stem changes (**jugaba**, **pensaba**, **contaba**) and no spelling changes."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only **nosotros** has a written accent: **-ábamos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Yo** and **él / ella** are identical (**trabajaba**). Add the pronoun or a name when it isn't clear."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-aba** is a wave that keeps rolling. **-é / -ó** (preterite) is the wave that breaks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "De joven, ==trabajaba== en un taller en Ensenada.",
              "en": "When I was young, I used to work at a shop in Ensenada."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Surfeabas== todos los días cuando vivías en Rosarito?",
              "en": "Did you surf every day when you lived in Rosarito?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi abuela ==cocinaba== frijoles cada domingo.",
              "en": "My grandma used to cook beans every Sunday."
            },
            {
              "es": "De niños, ==jugábamos== fútbol en la calle.",
              "en": "As kids, we used to play soccer in the street."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mis papás ==plantaban== maíz en el rancho.",
              "en": "My parents used to plant corn on the ranch."
            },
            {
              "es": "Yo ==estudiaba== cuando sonó el teléfono.",
              "en": "I was studying when the phone rang."
            },
            {
              "es": "Antes ==entrenaban== en un gimnasio pequeño.",
              "en": "They used to train in a small gym."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ==hablaban== inglés en la casa?",
              "en": "Did you guys speak English at home?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
